# The bash bootstrap installer is a Release artifact consumed on macOS:
# it must carry LF line endings regardless of the committer's platform
# (CRLF would break the shebang and every line continuation).
scripts/bootstrap/*.sh text eol=lf

# Every git-tracked file that ends up inside a published TGZ is pinned to LF.
#
# Found while cutting v0.2.0-rc.4: the same commit packed in two checkouts of
# this repository produced two different TGZ digests. The only difference was
# line endings — THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md was LF in one and CRLF in the other,
# cordis.patch.yml differed by one CR — because core.autocrlf=true leaves the
# working-tree bytes up to each checkout's history, and only the bootstrap
# scripts above were pinned.
#
# That breaks two promises at once. The installers embed a digest of the TGZ,
# so which checkout packed the release decides whether a rebuild matches; and
# docs/INSTALL.md § Advanced tells auditors to build from source and compare
# against the published hash, which cannot succeed while the bytes depend on
# the machine. Pinning these makes the pack reproducible from any clone.
packages/*/cordis.patch.yml text eol=lf
packages/*/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md text eol=lf
packages/*/README.md text eol=lf
packages/*/LICENSE text eol=lf
